<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ilergetes</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 205 BCE (approx.) · capital Iltirta</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The leading Iberian people of the Lleida plain, whose chiefs Indibilis and Mandonius switched between Carthage and Rome in the Second Punic War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ilergetes occupied the plains of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segre">Segre</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cinca">Cinca</a> rivers around modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> from the 5th century BCE, with their capital at Iltirta. By the late 3rd century BCE they were among the most powerful peoples of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were ruled by princes who could raise large armies and dominate neighbouring peoples. Their economy rested on the cereal plains of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segre">Segre</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Iltirta</a> minted coins with an Iberian legend. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a> their leaders <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indibilis">Indibilis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandonius">Mandonius</a> first served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, then joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-africanus">Scipio</a> in 209 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 206 and 205 BCE the brothers revolted against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indibilis">Indibilis</a> died in battle and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandonius">Mandonius</a> was handed over and executed. The Ilergetes were absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Iltirta</a> became Roman Ilerda, where Caesar defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legatus">legates</a> in 49 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 500 BCE – 205 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:49.75%;width:5.87%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 BCE – 205 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Iltirta</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Indibilis, Mandonius</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iberian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Iberian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ilergetans</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-352&amp;focus=ilergetes" aria-label="Ilergetes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4572 745 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ilergetes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5031 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4892 1001h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4892 1001h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Spain. <a href="/atlas?year=-352&amp;focus=ilergetes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

